# Model fragment shaders. Each line below is one shader. The build compiles
# all of them from scene_pbr_mesh_impl.hlsli and writes each one to
# <name>.frag.
#
# A name is "scene_pbr_mesh" followed by one word per feature, in this order:
#
#   mask or blend   alpha-tested or blended materials
#   screen          primitives that show a screen
#   ibl             lighting from an environment map
#   probes          lighting from the model's probes and an environment map
#   mirror          a lighter version of probes, for the floor's mirrored view
#   anim            material animation
#   details         material animation with detail layers
#   list            uses the instance's light list instead of the light clusters
#   debug           debug views (only built with AERON_DEBUG_UI)
#
# To add a shader, add a line here.
#
# To add a feature, pick a word and use it in the names here. The build then
# defines AERON_PBR_WORD_<WORD> for those shaders: use it in
# scene_pbr_mesh_impl.hlsli. Also add AERON_PBR_FEATURE_<WORD> to
# PbrMeshFeature in src/scene/pbr.c, which finds shaders by their features.

scene_pbr_mesh
scene_pbr_mesh_list
scene_pbr_mesh_anim
scene_pbr_mesh_anim_list
scene_pbr_mesh_details
scene_pbr_mesh_details_list
scene_pbr_mesh_mask
scene_pbr_mesh_mask_list
scene_pbr_mesh_mask_anim
scene_pbr_mesh_mask_anim_list
scene_pbr_mesh_mask_details
scene_pbr_mesh_mask_details_list
